{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"numerator numerator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","fileName":"Numerator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Numerator","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Fractions and Decimal Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Fraction","Denominator","Improper Fraction","Common Denominator","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"numerator numerator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","fileName":"Numerator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Numerator","heading":"Numerator","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The numerator is the upper component (m) of a [[Fraction]] (m/n). It records how many of the equal parts determined by the denominator are being taken and serves as the dividend in the equivalent division (m\\div n).\n\nA numerator may be larger than the [[Denominator]], producing an [[Improper Fraction]]. In fraction multiplication, numerators multiply with numerators. In addition or subtraction, numerators can be combined directly only after the fractions have been expressed with a [[Common Denominator]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Fraction","Denominator","Improper Fraction","Common Denominator","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"numerator numerator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Numerator.md","fileName":"